From cb013c91de2f3a4cce3e26527b13937ebb44266c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Mar 2026 01:11:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] rw-system.sh: fix MTK display on devices without fbdev or
 mtk_common HWC

Widen the MTK HWComposer bring-up mode detection to cover all MTK
platforms (ro.board.platform matching mt*) rather than only devices
with hwcomposer.mtk_common.so present.  Many MTK devices (e.g. TCL
on MT6765) use a different HWC module name but suffer from the same
DRM plane initialisation failure when the kernel lacks
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION.

Promote non-threaded RenderEngine backends to their threaded
equivalents.  Android 16 removed non-threaded backend support; vendor
partitions that set debug.renderengine.backend to skiagl or skiavk
cause SurfaceFlinger to crash and restart on every boot.  Use
resetprop_phh rather than setprop to bypass potential SELinux
property_service denials from the default exec context.  Only the
affected values are changed; devices that use the default auto-detect
or already set a threaded backend are left untouched.

Also guard the trailing goodix sysfs write behind an existence check
so it cannot fail the script's exit status on devices without a goodix
touchscreen.
---
 rw-system.sh | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rw-system.sh b/rw-system.sh
index f74604e..09bea47 100644
--- a/rw-system.sh
+++ b/rw-system.sh
@@ -1120,6 +1120,33 @@ if [ "$board" = mt6768 ]; then
 	setprop ro.netflix.bsp_rev MTK6768-19055-1
 fi
 
+# MTK HWComposer DRM plane and RenderEngine fixes.
+# On many MTK devices the vendor kernel DRM driver does not expose the
+# standard KMS atomic plane properties (alpha, pixel blend mode).  The
+# HWC then fails to initialise any overlay plane, atomic commits fail,
+# and the display stays black.  Setting ro.vendor.mtk_ovl_bringup=1
+# switches the HWC to its bring-up fallback path (GPU composition only),
+# bypassing the plane property checks.
+# The reliable runtime signal is the absence of /dev/fb0: kernels built
+# with CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=n create no fb node, and those same
+# kernels also lack the standard KMS atomic plane properties.  On
+# devices where plane init succeeds, /dev/fb0 is present.
+if echo "$board" | grep -qiE '^mt[0-9]'; then
+	if [ ! -e /dev/fb0 ]; then
+		resetprop_phh ro.vendor.mtk_ovl_bringup 1
+	fi
+fi
+
+# Android 16 removed support for non-threaded RenderEngine backends.
+# Some vendor partitions set debug.renderengine.backend to "skiagl" or
+# "skiavk" (the non-threaded variants), which causes SurfaceFlinger to
+# crash on every boot.  Promote to the threaded equivalent if needed.
+re_backend="$(getprop debug.renderengine.backend)"
+case "$re_backend" in
+	skiagl)   resetprop_phh debug.renderengine.backend skiaglthreaded ;;
+	skiavk)   resetprop_phh debug.renderengine.backend skiavkthreaded ;;
+esac
+
 if [ "$board" = lahaina ]; then
 	setprop ro.netflix.bsp_rev Q875-32774-1
 fi
@@ -1300,4 +1327,6 @@ if getprop ro.vendor.build.fingerprint | grep -iq -e Rebecco/K70_ROW; then
 fi
 
 # Enable pen mode on Lenovo/goodix
-echo 1 > /sys/devices/platform/goodix_ts.0/support_pen
+if [ -e /sys/devices/platform/goodix_ts.0/support_pen ]; then
+    echo 1 > /sys/devices/platform/goodix_ts.0/support_pen
+fi
